    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Au cas où",
     "texto": [
      "**Au cas où** (just in case) introduces a possibility: **Prends un parapluie au cas où il pleuvrait** (take an umbrella in case it rains).",
      "In careful standard usage it is followed by the conditional, even when the main sentence is in the present or the imperative."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Sinon",
     "texto": [
      "**Sinon** (otherwise) indicates what will happen if you do not do something: **Prends un parapluie, sinon tu seras trempé** (take an umbrella, otherwise you will get soaked)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
